    <statement><p>Evaluate the function at the specified points.</p>
<p><m>f(x,y) = y+xy^{3}, \left(2,5\right), \left(-1,3\right), \left(-2,2\right)</m></p>
<p>At <m>\left(2,5\right)</m>: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>At <m>\left(-1,3\right)</m>: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p>At <m>\left(-2,2\right)</m>: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>255</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-24</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-14</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>(x,y) = \left(2,5\right)</m> to find 
<m>f(2,5) = 5  + 2(5)^{3} = 255</m>.



Similarly, with <m>(x,y) = \left(-1,3\right)</m> we find 
<m>f(-1,3) = 3   - 1(3)^{3} = -24</m>.



Finally, for <m>(x,y) = \left(-2,2\right)</m> we find 
<m>f(-2,2) = 2   - 2(2)^{3} = -14</m>.


</solution>
